---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ContactConfiguration from '../components/ContactConfiguration.astro';

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
const description =
  'Personal website of Julian Pielmaier — computer science, machine learning, graphs, time series, and current research.';
---

<BaseLayout title="Julian Pielmaier — junipiel" description={description}>
  <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>

  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="wordmark" href="/" aria-label="junipiel home">
      <span class="wordmark__mark" aria-hidden="true">j</span>
      <span>junipiel</span>
    </a>

    <nav class="site-nav" aria-label="Main navigation">
      <a href="#current">Now</a>
      <a href="#interests">Interests</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/junipiel" rel="me noreferrer">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </nav>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero__copy">
        <h1 id="hero-title">Hi, I’m Julian.</h1>
        <p class="hero__text hero__text--primary">
          I came into machine learning through the engineering side of computer science. Building systems is
          still part of what I enjoy, but over time I’ve moved closer to research: the “why” behind a method is
          usually what keeps me thinking.
        </p>
        <p class="hero__text">
          My work keeps circling back to structured data—relations in graphs, change in time series, and the
          models that try to make sense of both.
        </p>

        <div class="wip-note">
          <span class="wip-note__label">Work in progress</span>
          <p>
            This is the first small version of this site. I’m building it into a personal notebook for ongoing
            work, projects, technical notes, and interactive experiments. A few things are deliberately still
            unfinished.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="https://github.com/junipiel" rel="me noreferrer">
            GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="button button--quiet" href="#current">
            What I’m working on <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero__visual">
        <ContactConfiguration />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="current" aria-labelledby="current-title">
      <div class="section__label" aria-hidden="true">01 / Now</div>
      <div class="section__content">
        <h2 id="current-title">What I’m working on</h2>
        <p class="section__lead">
          At the moment I split my time between my master’s thesis and my work as a research assistant.
        </p>

        <div class="work-list">
          <article class="work-item">
            <div class="work-item__meta">Master’s thesis · ongoing</div>
            <h3>From contact graphs to sphere configurations</h3>
            <p>
              Given a combinatorial contact graph, how can we construct a valid 3D arrangement of equal
              spheres? I’m comparing classical geometric methods with learned models and hybrid solver
              pipelines. What interests me most is what relational information the models learn, why their
              predictions make useful solver starts, and when learning actually adds something.
            </p>
            <p class="work-item__context">
              For this thesis, I’m a visiting researcher at MPI MiS in Leipzig.
            </p>
          </article>

          <article class="work-item work-item--compact">
            <div class="work-item__meta">Research assistant · ongoing</div>
            <h3>Project KORALLE</h3>
            <p>
              Alongside my thesis, I work as a research assistant at InfAI on the KORALLE project.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" id="interests" aria-labelledby="interests-title">
      <div class="section__label" aria-hidden="true">02 / Interests</div>
      <div class="section__content">
        <h2 id="interests-title">Questions I keep coming back to</h2>
        <p class="section__lead">
          The common thread is structure and explanation: how relationships and temporal patterns can be
          represented, what models extract from them, and where learned methods genuinely improve on strong
          classical approaches.
        </p>

        <ul class="threads">
          <li>
            <span class="threads__title">Relations</span>
            <span>Graphs, relational representations, and the geometry hidden in connections.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="threads__title">Dynamics</span>
            <span>Time series, streaming data, and systems that change over time.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="threads__title">Learning</span>
            <span>Machine learning for structured problems, often together with classical algorithms.</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="threads__title">Understanding</span>
            <span>Why a model works, what it has learned, and when it fails.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="direction-title">
      <div class="section__label" aria-hidden="true">03 / This site</div>
      <div class="section__content">
        <h2 id="direction-title">Still taking shape</h2>
        <p class="section__lead">
          I want this to become a useful record of the things I’m learning and building—not a polished list
          of claims. The next pieces will appear as they become worth sharing.
        </p>

        <ul class="roadmap">
          <li>
            <span class="roadmap__title">Project pages</span>
            <span>Code, results, dead ends, and enough context to make them useful.</span>
            <span class="roadmap__status">In progress</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="roadmap__title">Notes</span>
            <span>Working notes on graphs, time series, geometry, and model behaviour.</span>
            <span class="roadmap__status">In progress</span>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="roadmap__title">Experiments</span>
            <span>Small interactive demos tied to questions I’m actually working on.</span>
            <span class="roadmap__status">In progress</span>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section section--last" aria-labelledby="elsewhere-title">
      <div class="section__label" aria-hidden="true">04 / Links</div>
      <div class="section__content">
        <h2 id="elsewhere-title">Links</h2>
        <a class="large-link" href="https://github.com/junipiel" rel="me noreferrer">
          <span>GitHub</span>
          <span class="large-link__handle">@junipiel</span>
          <span class="large-link__arrow" aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="site-footer">
    <span>© {year} Julian Pielmaier</span>
    <span>junipiel.com</span>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
